From b41601bf6df471262f8d8e4e5a823d0eff239d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deano Calver <me@deanoc.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:22:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] DE25 managed shell: remove the vendor on-chip memory and
 disable the full HPS-to-FPGA bridge

The GHRD on-chip memory (ocm, 16384 x 128 bits) was the only responder on
the full HPS-to-FPGA bridge and nothing in FES addresses it. Remove it from
the managed fabric and select H2F_Width=0 (Unused) so the bridge has no
fabric interface. managed-scanout-initiators moves to v4; the verifier now
refuses the memory, its route and the bridge ports instead of requiring them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
